{"type":"message","id":"b6ffbc54","parentId":"a7b7a4b9","timestamp":"2026-05-02T07:13:32.147Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"process_1777705938566_22","toolName":"process","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"CLARITY Act Stablecoin Regulation\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"CLARITY Act crypto\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"CLARITY Act Stablecoin Yield Rules Finalized: ‘Go Time’ For Crypto Bill\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinTelegraph\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/go-time-after-clarity-act-stablecoin-yield-compromise-finalized\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"The US CLARITY Act's new stablecoin yield provisions have been finalized and published.\",\n    \"The act prohibits paying interest for solely holding stablecoins but allows rewards for 'bona fide activities'.\",\n    \"Coinbase chief legal officer Faryar Shirzad stated, 'It’s time to get CLARITY done.'\",\n    \"Polymarket traders see a 55% chance of the CLARITY Act being signed into law in 2026.\",\n    \"Galaxy Digital's Alex Thorn expects the Senate Banking Committee to schedule a markup 'imminently'.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: CLARITY Act Stablecoin Yield Rules Finalized: ‘Go Time’ For Crypto Bill\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/go-time-after-clarity-act-stablecoin-yield-compromise-finalized\\n\\nPublished Time: Sat, 02 May 2026 06:25:50 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nThe US CLARITY Act, which aims to provide the US crypto industry with more regulatory clarity, could now move closer to becoming law after new stablecoin yield provisions were published, according to Coinbase chief legal officer Faryar Shirzad.\\n\\n“It’s time to get CLARITY done,” Shirzad [said](https://x.com/faryarshirzad/status/2050325150747484421?s=20) in an X post on Friday, after US Senator Thom Tillis and US Senator Angela Alsobrooks published the final text aimed at settling the stablecoin yield dispute between the banking and crypto industries, which has centered on whether such yields would harm the banking system’s competitiveness.\\n\\n“In the end, the banks were able to get more restrictions on rewards, but we protected what matters – the ability for Americans to earn rewards, based on real usage of crypto platforms and networks,” Shirzad said.\\n\\n![Image 1](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/Screen%20Shot%202026-05-02%20at%201.09.20%20am.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Extract of the “SEC 404. Prohibiting interest and yield on payment stablecoins” document. Source:_[_Alex Thorn_](https://x.com/intangiblecoins/status/2050331780226355426?s=20)\\n\\nThe text titled “SEC 404. Prohibiting interest and yield on payment stablecoins” states that no crypto firm may pay “any form of interest or yield” to customers solely for holding stablecoins, akin to a bank deposit or any similar interest-bearing product.\\n\\n![Image 2](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=807,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/Screen%20Shot%202026-05-02%20at%201.20.56%20am.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Source:_[_Patrick Witt_](https://x.com/patrickjwitt/status/2050327616628969623?s=20)\\n\\nHowever, it allows firms to offer rewards tied to “bona fide activities.” Some industry executives voiced frustration with the ruling. Helius Labs CEO Mert Mumtaz [said](https://cointelegraph.com/news/https%252525253A%252525252F%252525252Fhttps%252525253A%252525252F%252525252Fx.com%252525252Fmert%252525252Fstatus%252525252F2050353943151030294%252525253Fs%252525253D20), \\\"The clarity of not getting risk-free yield on your dollars without using a bank.\\\"\\n\\n## Polymarket traders anticipate 55% odds of CLARITY passing in 2026\\n\\nIt marks a significant step forward for both the legislation and the broader crypto industry, as the stablecoin yield debate had been one of the main roadblocks delaying its passage, despite expectations earlier this year that it would move through Congress.\\n\\n![Image 3](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=817,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/Screen%20Shot%202026-05-02%20at%201.11.43%20am.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Source:_[_Toly Yakovenko_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/https%252525253A%252525252F%252525252Fhttps%252525253A%252525252F%252525252Fx.com%252525252Ftoly%252525252Fstatus%252525252F2050351841427493200%252525253Fs%252525253D20)\\n\\n“Now that this issue is behind us, it’s time to focus on the broader bill,” Shirzad said.\\n\\nTraders on the Polymarket crypto prediction market now [see](https://polymarket.com/event/clarity-act-signed-into-law-in-2026) a 55% chance of the CLARITY Act being signed into law in 2026, up 9% over the past 24 hours.\\n\\nMany in the industry are now calling for the bill to be marked up. Coinbase CEO Brian Armstrong [said](https://x.com/brian_armstrong/status/2050325975226081308?s=20) shortly after the announcement, “Mark it up.”\\n\\n## Senate Banking Committee could schedule markup “imminently”\\n\\nGalaxy Digital head of firmwide research Alex Thorn [said](https://x.com/intangiblecoins/status/2050331780226355426?s=20) the “release of text suggests that Senate Banking will schedule markup imminently, as soon as the week of May 11.”\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**Spot Bitcoin ETF outflows top $490M: Is BTC’s rally losing momentum?**_](https://cointelegraph.com/markets/spot-bitcoin-etf-outflows-top-490m-is-btcs-rally-losing-momentum?utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound&utm_medium=rss&utm_source=rss_feed)\\n\\nHowever, Thorn [warned](https://x.com/intangiblecoins/status/2050335032481317317?s=20) that he expects “the banks to increase their opposition efforts.”\\n\\nUS Senator Bernie Moreno recently [said](https://x.com/EleanorTerrett/status/2047096824662507635?s=20) that he anticipates the CLARITY Act to “get done” by the end of May. On April 11, US Senator Cynthia Lummis [said](https://x.com/SenLummis/status/2042955324274151624?s=20), “It’s now or never.”\\n\\n_**Magazine:**_[_**Why is Ethereum Foundation selling? BTC futures warning signs: Ma\"\n}\n```\n\nProcess exited with code 0."}],"details":{"status":"completed","sessionId":"quick-cedar","exitCode":0,"aggregated":"```json\n{\n  \"topic_theme\": \"CLARITY Act Stablecoin Regulation\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"CLARITY Act crypto\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"CLARITY Act Stablecoin Yield Rules Finalized: ‘Go Time’ For Crypto Bill\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"CoinTelegraph\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/go-time-after-clarity-act-stablecoin-yield-compromise-finalized\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"The US CLARITY Act's new stablecoin yield provisions have been finalized and published.\",\n    \"The act prohibits paying interest for solely holding stablecoins but allows rewards for 'bona fide activities'.\",\n    \"Coinbase chief legal officer Faryar Shirzad stated, 'It’s time to get CLARITY done.'\",\n    \"Polymarket traders see a 55% chance of the CLARITY Act being signed into law in 2026.\",\n    \"Galaxy Digital's Alex Thorn expects the Senate Banking Committee to schedule a markup 'imminently'.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Title: CLARITY Act Stablecoin Yield Rules Finalized: ‘Go Time’ For Crypto Bill\\n\\nURL Source: https://cointelegraph.com/news/go-time-after-clarity-act-stablecoin-yield-compromise-finalized\\n\\nPublished Time: Sat, 02 May 2026 06:25:50 GMT\\n\\nMarkdown Content:\\nThe US CLARITY Act, which aims to provide the US crypto industry with more regulatory clarity, could now move closer to becoming law after new stablecoin yield provisions were published, according to Coinbase chief legal officer Faryar Shirzad.\\n\\n“It’s time to get CLARITY done,” Shirzad [said](https://x.com/faryarshirzad/status/2050325150747484421?s=20) in an X post on Friday, after US Senator Thom Tillis and US Senator Angela Alsobrooks published the final text aimed at settling the stablecoin yield dispute between the banking and crypto industries, which has centered on whether such yields would harm the banking system’s competitiveness.\\n\\n“In the end, the banks were able to get more restrictions on rewards, but we protected what matters – the ability for Americans to earn rewards, based on real usage of crypto platforms and networks,” Shirzad said.\\n\\n![Image 1](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=896,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/Screen%20Shot%202026-05-02%20at%201.09.20%20am.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Extract of the “SEC 404. Prohibiting interest and yield on payment stablecoins” document. Source:_[_Alex Thorn_](https://x.com/intangiblecoins/status/2050331780226355426?s=20)\\n\\nThe text titled “SEC 404. Prohibiting interest and yield on payment stablecoins” states that no crypto firm may pay “any form of interest or yield” to customers solely for holding stablecoins, akin to a bank deposit or any similar interest-bearing product.\\n\\n![Image 2](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=807,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/Screen%20Shot%202026-05-02%20at%201.20.56%20am.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Source:_[_Patrick Witt_](https://x.com/patrickjwitt/status/2050327616628969623?s=20)\\n\\nHowever, it allows firms to offer rewards tied to “bona fide activities.” Some industry executives voiced frustration with the ruling. Helius Labs CEO Mert Mumtaz [said](https://cointelegraph.com/news/https%252525253A%252525252F%252525252Fhttps%252525253A%252525252F%252525252Fx.com%252525252Fmert%252525252Fstatus%252525252F2050353943151030294%252525253Fs%252525253D20), \\\"The clarity of not getting risk-free yield on your dollars without using a bank.\\\"\\n\\n## Polymarket traders anticipate 55% odds of CLARITY passing in 2026\\n\\nIt marks a significant step forward for both the legislation and the broader crypto industry, as the stablecoin yield debate had been one of the main roadblocks delaying its passage, despite expectations earlier this year that it would move through Congress.\\n\\n![Image 3](https://resizer.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/f=auto,onerror=redirect,w=817,q=90/https://payload.cointelegraph.com/api/media/file/Screen%20Shot%202026-05-02%20at%201.11.43%20am.png?prefix=media%2Fcontent)\\n_Source:_[_Toly Yakovenko_](https://cointelegraph.com/news/https%252525253A%252525252F%252525252Fhttps%252525253A%252525252F%252525252Fx.com%252525252Ftoly%252525252Fstatus%252525252F2050351841427493200%252525253Fs%252525253D20)\\n\\n“Now that this issue is behind us, it’s time to focus on the broader bill,” Shirzad said.\\n\\nTraders on the Polymarket crypto prediction market now [see](https://polymarket.com/event/clarity-act-signed-into-law-in-2026) a 55% chance of the CLARITY Act being signed into law in 2026, up 9% over the past 24 hours.\\n\\nMany in the industry are now calling for the bill to be marked up. Coinbase CEO Brian Armstrong [said](https://x.com/brian_armstrong/status/2050325975226081308?s=20) shortly after the announcement, “Mark it up.”\\n\\n## Senate Banking Committee could schedule markup “imminently”\\n\\nGalaxy Digital head of firmwide research Alex Thorn [said](https://x.com/intangiblecoins/status/2050331780226355426?s=20) the “release of text suggests that Senate Banking will schedule markup imminently, as soon as the week of May 11.”\\n\\n_**Related:**_[_**Spot Bitcoin ETF outflows top $490M: Is BTC’s rally losing momentum?**_](https://cointelegraph.com/markets/spot-bitcoin-etf-outflows-top-490m-is-btcs-rally-losing-momentum?utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound&utm_medium=rss&utm_source=rss_feed)\\n\\nHowever, Thorn [warned](https://x.com/intangiblecoins/status/2050335032481317317?s=20) that he expects “the banks to increase their opposition efforts.”\\n\\nUS Senator Bernie Moreno recently [said](https://x.com/EleanorTerrett/status/2047096824662507635?s=20) that he anticipates the CLARITY Act to “get done” by the end of May. On April 11, US Senator Cynthia Lummis [said](https://x.com/SenLummis/status/2042955324274151624?s=20), “It’s now or never.”\\n\\n_**Magazine:**_[_**Why is Ethereum Foundation selling? BTC futures warning signs: Ma\"\n}\n```\n","name":"rm ~/.openclaw/agents/res...sessions/sessions.json"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1777706012147}}
