{"type":"message","id":"a4585452","parentId":"836753e5","timestamp":"2026-05-03T19:01:27.425Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"We need to run the pipeline again. The previous run succeeded. We must execute the full pipeline steps again: research, write, image, publish. Ensure we clear sessions each time. Use same steps as before. Possibly need to ensure we don't reuse previous files that might cause conflicts. Should delete previous article files and image maybe. Use same commands. We'll start fresh: remove researcher sessions, run researcher, capture output. We'll store RESEARCH_JSON.json again (overwrites). Then writer using file read method. Then creator generate image. Then publish. We'll need to poll each step.\n\nProceed stepwise.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"**Starting a fresh pipeline run** – clearing the researcher session and invoking the researcher agent to fetch the latest crypto news. I'll monitor the output and store it as `RESEARCH_JSON.json` for the next steps."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tooluse_O97TgALwfEfuR3PrE0hbH2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"rm -f ~/.openclaw/agents/researcher/sessions/sessions.json && openclaw agent --agent researcher --message \"Follow your SOUL to cross-reference multiple RSS feeds, find the single biggest news event, and extract deep facts. Return the aggregated Single-Topic JSON.\" --deliver"}}],"api":"bedrock-converse-stream","provider":"amazon-bedrock","model":"openai.gpt-oss-120b-1:0","usage":{"input":32150,"output":251,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":32401,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1777834880032}}
